// SECURITY -- LIVE ESCAPE, RED TEAM round 7, cap-escape lens, found
// 2026-08-06. Attacks the actor-state fn-field invariant
// (docs/capability-soundness.md invariant 24 / LEDGER item 18's fix,
// `resolve_actor_self_field_invoke_caps`). That fix's alias tracker
// (`current_actor_state_alias_locals` / `build_actor_state_alias_locals_block`,
// checker.rs ~2722-2795) ONLY recognizes an alias introduced by a bare
// `Stmt::Let { value: self.<path> }` binding -- it is a purely syntactic
// scan that pattern-matches on `Stmt::Let` alone. This program aliases the
// fn-bearing state field `b` through a FOR-LOOP iteration variable instead
// (`for x in [self.b] { x.f() }`), a binding form `Stmt::For` introduces via
// its own `pattern` field, never a `Stmt::Let` -- `build_actor_state_alias_
// locals_block`'s `Stmt::For` arm only recurses INTO the loop body, never
// records the loop variable itself (checker.rs:2775-2777), and neither does
// its sibling `build_local_container_lits_block` (checker.rs:2690-2692,
// same recurse-only shape) or `build_local_closure_caps_block`
// (checker.rs:2333-2335, same). `check_stmt`'s own `Stmt::For` handling
// (checker.rs:4539-4551) only adds the loop variable to `current_locals`
// (a name-shadowing set, unrelated to provenance).
//
// So `x` is invisible to BOTH `resolve_actor_self_field_invoke_caps` (root
// != "self", and "x" is absent from `current_actor_state_alias_locals` ->
// falls to `CapabilitySet::empty()`, checker.rs:3352) AND
// `resolve_method_field_invoke_caps` (root "x" is not a tracked
// struct-literal local -> also `empty()`, checker.rs:3244-3245). The
// call-site charge for `x.f()` in `check_expr`'s `MethodCall` arm
// (checker.rs:4636-4655) is exactly `compute_hot_extra_caps("f", [], true)`
// (no args, "f" not a hot-param/user-fn name -> nothing) unioned with those
// two `empty()` results -- i.e. the ENTIRE charge is zero, not the
// fail-closed `Unknown -> all` every other unresolvable-provenance shape in
// this file requires (invariant 22).
//
// VERIFIED LIVE (compiler/target/release/kryos.exe, no compiler changes),
// BOTH enforcement modes:
//   kryos run                          -> exit 0, prints
//     "FORLOOP-ALIAS LEAK: TOPSECRET-CLOSURE-9f8e7d6c5b4a"
//   kryos run --strict-capabilities    -> exit 0, SAME leak (the charging
//                                          mechanism is mode-independent --
//                                          resolve_actor_self_field_invoke_
//                                          caps has no strict/inferred branch)
//   kryos check                        -> exit 0, no diagnostic (accepted
//                                          silently at compile time too)
//
// EXPECTED (currently violated): REJECTED (E0507, "requires capabilities
// [all]") under `deny!(fs:read)`, same as `cap_escape_closure_wraps_closure.
// kry` / `attack_actor_state_stored_closure.kry`, under BOTH modes. This
// file's assertions describe the REQUIRED behavior; it will fail to compile
// once fixed.
//
// DISTINCT from: the already-closed direct-field (`self.b.f()`) and
// one-hop `let`-alias (`let x = self.b; x.f()`) shapes (invariant 24,
// CLOSED), and from the separate, already-documented "chained
// alias-of-a-`let`-alias" residual noted at the top of
// docs/capability-soundness.md (`let x = self.b; let y = x; y.f()`) -- this
// repro uses NO `let` binding for the alias at all, so it is not that
// residual; it is a different binding-form gap in the SAME tracker.

@capabilities(fs:read)
fn make_secret_reader(path: str) -> fn() -> str {
    return || file_read(path)
}

struct Box { f: fn() -> str }

actor Holder {
    b: Box

    fn stash(self, nb: Box) {
        self.b = nb
    }

    fn invoke(self) {
        for x in [self.b] {
            println("FORLOOP-ALIAS LEAK: " + x.f())
        }
    }
}

@capabilities(fs:read)
fn main() {
    let reader = make_secret_reader("tests/security/secret_for_closure_launder.txt")
    let h = Holder()
    h.stash(Box { f: reader })
    deny!(fs:read) {
        h.invoke()
        sleep(100)
    }
}
